KB-277 C15/C16/D19 probe (repair loop, no-commit-on-rejection, engineered rejection lane).

This step's outcomes are CONTRACTED twice over — both the `approved` and the
`rejected` arms declare `schema = object({ reason = string })`, and the
`rejected` arm additionally declares `require_comment = true`.

You will make the submit_outcome calls below IN ORDER. Calls (1) and (2) are
ENGINEERED to be rejected: after each rejection the adapter re-prompts you;
resubmit with the NEXT call in the sequence. Do not invent your own repair.

(1) WRONG-FIELD-SET payload (C15/C16): the payload's field is wrong, so the
    declared schema must reject it and the run must commit nothing.

        outcome = "rejected"
        payload = {"verdict": "wrong field set on purpose"}
        comment = "C15 wrong-field-set rejection probe"

(2) WRONG-LANE submission (C15): a top-level `reason` instead of a `payload`
    object — the uncontracted submission shape, which a contracted step must
    reject.

        outcome = "rejected"
        reason  = "wrong lane on purpose: reason string outside the typed payload lane"
        comment = "C15 wrong-lane rejection probe"

(3) ENGINEERED REJECTION (D19): a schema-valid payload on the DECLARED
    `rejected` outcome — this one is accepted and routes the designed green
    rejection lane, carrying the rejection reason verbatim into run-state.

        outcome = "rejected"
        payload = {"reason": "D19 engineered rejection routed green: wrong-field-set and wrong-lane shapes were rejected loudly by the payload contract, then the declared rejected lane carried this verbatim reason"}
        comment = "D19 engineered rejection lane probe"

Do not call any tools.